{
 "titulo": "Pixar Was Sold for $5 Million 🎬",
 "texto_pantalla": "$5 MILLION",
 "lote": "M2026112102",
 "tema": "mdm",
 "marca": "MILLION DOLLAR MISTAKE",
 "acento": "#5effa1",
 "nota_datos": "Lucas vendió la división gráfica de Lucasfilm tras su divorcio de 1983; pidió ~US$30 M sin compradores (AOL/GOBankingRates). Jobs pagó US$5 M y puso US$5 M más de capital, 3-feb-1986 (Cord Cutters, CNN Money; Biography: US$10 M en total). Disney compró Pixar por ~US$7.400 M en acciones, ene/may 2006 (CNN Money, Cord Cutters). 7.400/10 = 740 veces.",
 "frases": [
  "In 1986, George Lucas sold a small computer team.",
  "After his divorce he needed cash. He asked for 30 million dollars, and nobody bought it.",
  "Then Steve Jobs paid 5 million, and put in 5 million more.",
  "The team was called Pixar.",
  "Twenty years later, Disney bought it for 7.4 billion dollars.",
  "That's 740 times what Jobs put in.",
  "Lesson: before you sell something, ask what it could become. Would you have sold it?",
  "Follow for the next million dollar mistake."
 ],
